00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
dealing a major  blow to the biden administration and  reinstating the remain in mexico policy  this after texas sued over the program  suspension claiming it placed a burden  on local governments forced to provide  services to immigrants texas attorney  general ken paxton was behind the  lawsuit and he joins us now live okay  ken so first off this program keeps  migrants in mexico as they await these  hearings especially right now with the  influx and the surge at the border and  not only that but the the surgeon  coveted cases how important is it for  them to remain in mexico while they  await these hearings  so incredibly important this is one of  president trump's i think greatest  successes because we he had the same  problem he instituted this program  because all of these immigrants were  being told by immigration lawyers hey  come to come to the united states you'll  cross the border tell a border agent  that you're claiming asylum  and then you get to disappear into the  country for years you don't ever have to  come back and so this idea that you have  to stay in mexico and wait for your  asylum hearing is a really good idea  especially when only about 14  of these people qualify so it was  greatly successful under the trump  administration we're hoping that  reinstituting it will really help along  the border and then i want to get to  this this is dhs's response to the  supreme court's ruling it says dhs has  appealed the district court's order and  will continue to vigorously challenge it  as the appeal process continues however  dhs will comply with the order in good  faith how long could this appeal process  take  you know it could take a long time but  because we would still have to go  through like like a little trial uh on  the merits of the case however we won a  preliminary injunction at the district  court level in federal court in texas we  then took it to the fifth circuit we won  again we took the us they took it to the  u.s supreme we won again  so when you do that the court is saying  you're like likely to win on the merits  and when they're granting an injunction  so i feel very confident that they can  appeal it and we can go through the  trial process but pretty sure we're  going to win and we already have the  injunction in place so we're fairly  confident we're going forward in the  right direction obviously it's important  for you know the safety of america for  people to to come into this this country  uh legally but  texas in particular right now how  important is it for just the state of  texas  oh it's it's incredible i just met with  a bunch of ranchers a couple days ago  and they are so frustrated they're so  fearful because they're they're not only  their property being destroyed but they  fear for their lives i met with the  leaders along the borders they're  fearful they don't know how to deal with  the influx they're worried about covet  killing their people they're worried  about the importation of fentanyl which  is dramatically up because of the border  crisis and human trafficking sex  trafficking all kinds of different  crimes so we have a lot of problems  related to this and a lot of obviously  massively increased law enforcement  costs along with health care costs so  yeah it has a dramatic effect impact on  our state and as they import these  people all over the country with covid  you know this is going to affect the  health and safety of citizens across the  country as these people are moved around  secretly by the administration  and and with this administration with  with biden's words um  do you think that the president  respects the rule of law especially when  it comes to states rights or is he  basically just saying i can do whatever  i want it doesn't matter you know about  statute or any of the rights of the  states  no there's no doubt he looks at the  federal laws is sort of his choice if he  wants to follow what has been passed by  congress his job is actually not to  change the laws it's to follow them  whether he likes them or not i have to  do the same thing in the executive  branch he doesn't do that he says look i  don't have to follow the laws i was  elected president this constitutional  thing doesn't work for me so he  literally tells people not to enforce  the law and that's what's happening  along the border that's we have such a  disaster and you can compare what donald  trump did a year ago to where we are now  the numbers are dramatically different  the results are horrible and it's  because we have a president who  literally is out of control  and then before we do let you go um just  to put it in context july 2020 there's  40  929 border encounters and then july of  2021 there was 212  672 just to put it in perspective and  then this number right here um over a  million um as far as border encounters  and fiscal year 2021. okay ken paxton  thanks for joining us we got to leave it  here but we appreciate your take on this  and good luck in texas  thank you

